    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_2bad9326",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: shoot_boy_i_ain_t_racist; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a young Black child sitting in the driver's seat of a car, looking surprised or confused. The overlaid text reads: 'shoot boy, i ain't racist' and 'i've got four black tires and a color tv.' This meme uses a racially charged, historically coded joke to mock the idea of being 'not racist' by making a crude, stereotypical comparison between Black people and 'black tires' (a reference to the color black, often used in racist stereotypes to imply inferiority or association with negative traits) and 'color TV' (a reference to the idea that Black people are 'primitive' or 'not modern' because they 'don't have color TV' — a stereotype that implies Black people are less advanced or less civilized). The meme is hateful because it relies on racist tropes and stereotypes to make its point, and it is intended to provoke laughter at the expense of Black people, reinforcing harmful racial biases. The child's innocent expression contrasts with the offensive text, which amplifies the shock value and the racist message. The overall intent is to spread and normalize racist humor by using a child as a visual punchline to a racially insensitive joke.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_302654b1"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
